<!--
  The 26 canonical public URLs, in the same trailing-slash form as the
  rel=canonical on each page.

  The host below is the production default. Builds resolve it from the same
  VITE_SITE_URL that canonical and og:url come from (vite.config.js), so a
  preview build cannot end up advertising production URLs, and the sitemap
  can never disagree with the canonicals.

  Deliberately absent: the error page and the form confirmation, which both
  carry a noindex tag; the extension-suffixed alternate of every page, each
  of which 301s to the clean URL above; and the 16 old WordPress paths that
  redirect here. No path appears literally in this comment, so a tool that
  greps the file rather than parsing it cannot mistake a note for an entry.

  lastmod is per page, not per build. Each date is the day of the last
  commit that changed THAT page's own source file, read from git history -
  so the dates differ, and a page that has not changed does not claim it
  has. A single build date across all 26 would be a lie Google learns to
  ignore.

  These are written out rather than generated at build time because the
  generator would need full git history in the build environment; a shallow
  clone would silently collapse every date onto one, which is the exact
  failure this avoids. The cost is that a content change must update the
  date here too.
-->
